    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d185-a1">

                <pb facs="0261" n="179" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg179"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Blumhe to Mr. Wood</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Copenhagen,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-06-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 9, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> In answer to your letter containing the
                    proclamation of the President of the United States of the 10th ultimo, relative
                    to the American insurgent cruisers, I hasten to inform you that the government
                    of the King has never recognized the so-called Confederate States as a
                    belligerent party, and consequently that proclamation will not affect the
                    conduct hitherto observed by the Danish authorities towards their cruisers. On
                    mentioning that this fact is well known to the cabinet in Washington, which has
                    often expressed satisfaction for it, to the minister of the King in that city, I
                    accept the occasion to repeat the assurance of my most distinguished
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>BLUMHE.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bradford R. Wood,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Resident of the United States.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
